# The environment WinT reads secrets from. Copy this to `.env`, fill it in, and
# load it into the shell you build or run from — `.env` itself is ignored by git
# and must never be committed.
#
# Nothing here is compiled into the app. Every value is read with
# `std::env::var` at the moment it is used, in Rust only: a webview that could
# see one of these could hand it to any page it later loads.

# The server-side key for the feedback broker, used by `src-tauri/src/feedback.rs`
# to authenticate `POST https://feedback.broker/api/ingest` with the
# `x-feedback-key` header.
#
# Optional. A build with this unset falls back to BUILT_IN_KEY in that file,
# which is what makes reporting work for an ordinary install - a packaged app
# does not inherit the environment of the shell that installed it.
#
# Set this when you want a different key than the one the binary carries: to use
# a rotated key without waiting for a build, or to point a dev machine at a
# separate workspace. Whatever is here wins over the built-in one.
FEEDBACK_BROKER_API_KEY=
